ov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b092e67b29472df648ea32d2432f2eb9c230c8e2.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 3:47PM MST until November 3 at 3:45PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"Flooding along the upper Conejos River continues.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by rain and snowmelt is expected to\ncontinue.\n\n* WHERE...Western Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 345 PM MST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the upper Conejos River, for areas below\nPlatoro and downstream through Mogote, will continue into Tuesday.\nResidual impacts from flooding of smaller creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations may continue. Numerous\nroads remain closed due to flooding. Low-water crossings are\ninundated with water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 343 PM MST, Rain and snowmelt from the previous 24 hours is\ncausing continued flooding.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Western Conejos County, from Platoro\ndownstream through Mogote.\n- http://www.water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-03T15:45:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.aac508d852d6aadc0ffc543722b1bf27c1ab74d4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.aac508d852d6aadc0ffc543722b1bf27c1ab74d4.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T11:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 031120 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 420 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Windy across the plains early today. - Unsettled pattern in place through Saturday. - Drier and warmer conditions return early next week. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH TONIGHT/... Issued at 125 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 Today - Tonight: For Tuesday, relatively quiet weather ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"